    "lawCode": "Amd §2801-d, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3841\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to retaliation by\nresidential health care facilities where a patient asserts a private\nright of action\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo improve protection of nursing home patients from retaliation for\nsuing the nursing home because of an injury.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nAmend § 2801-d(10) of the Public Health Law to prohibit discrimination\nagainst a patient when the patient's legal representative sues a\nnursing home or its employee for alleged injury.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nNone.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nFollowing the 1975 massive scandal of fraud and abuse in nursing\nhomes, public Health Law §280 1-d was enacted to give patients\nincreased powers to enforce their right to adequate treatment and care\nby providing them the right to sue for damages and other relief.\n\nSubdivision 10 (a) of section 2801-d protects nursing home patients\nfrom discrimination when they allege injury in a lawsuit. This bill\nwill extend that protection to encompass the situation where the\npatient's cause is taken up by a representative, where the patient is\nunable to act on his or her own behalf.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
